Top-down battle map of a rectangular wine cellar beneath an abandoned laundry building. D&D grid style, 5ft squares visible. Approximately 30x20 feet.

LAYOUT:
- NORTH: wooden staircase descending from above (trapdoor open at top). The stairs creak.
- CENTER: a single wooden chair, slightly off-center. Ropes on the floor around it (for tying a prisoner).
- SOUTH: a secondary door (heavy wood, iron hinges) leading to a narrow alley outside.
- EAST WALL: row of empty wine barrels stacked two high. Provides half cover.
- WEST WALL: wooden crates (some open, some sealed). A small table with a lantern, rope, and a knife.
- CORNERS: cobwebs, puddles of water, crumbling mortar between stones.

DETAILS:
- One iron lantern hanging from a ceiling hook (center-north), casting a pool of warm light.
- Stone walls, damp, with green moss near the floor.
- Low ceiling (7 feet) — claustrophobic feel.
- Floor: packed earth with scattered straw.
- A bucket in the corner (interrogation scene detail).

LIGHTING: Single lantern creates bright light in center 15ft radius, dim light to the walls. Corners are in shadow.

STYLE: Classic D&D battle map, top-down, clean grid lines, muted earth tones (grey stone, brown wood, dark shadows). Furniture shown as simple colored shapes. No characters.

SIZE: 120x75 feet (24x15 squares).
